      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For those who are not familiar with Japanese IME (Input Method Editor):\nEnter key means \"Select the focused candidate\" in the \"Conversion candidate window\" of Japanese IME (see https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/microsoft-japanese-ime-da40471d-6b91-4042-ae8b-713a96476916 under \"Conversion candidate window\" )\nTechnically speaking the text input UI wrongly handles Enter key input as its own \"complete\" action. It should not do that while IME is active.\nPossible workaround is clicking somewhere outside of inputting text under (being handled by) IME. But that isn't normal operation and it's uncomfortable.\nInfo for Japanese users:\n変換中の文字列以外の所をクリックすれば、さしあたりの回避は可能です。",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
